    {
        "content": "<p>macovedj edited <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14443\">PR #14443</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Currently, if a client resets after its connection is accepted, <code>remote-address</code> can fail because we query the socket again instead of keeping the address returned by <code>accept</code>. This PR preserves that address so it can still be accessed after a reset.<br>\nI also updated <code>cargo-fuzz</code> because installing the pinned version from scratch was failing in CI.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 627556286,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1790629174
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> pchickey submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14443#pullrequestreview-5344617794\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 627557205,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1790629402
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> pchickey created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14443#discussion_r4127009109\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In this case (implicitly, <code>accepted_peer: None</code>), if stream.peer_addr() succeeds, wouldn't we want to save the peer address in accepted_peer? (That would require the whole method to become &amp;mut self). And in that case, we could rename the struct member to <code>peer</code>, dropping the <code>accepted</code>?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 627557208,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1790629402
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>macovedj updated <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14443\">PR #14443</a>.</p>",
        "id": 627562768,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1790631028
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> macovedj submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14443#pullrequestreview-5344913148\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 627563569,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1790631264
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> macovedj created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14443#discussion_r4127239227\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Ah yeah, I only cached the address returned by <code>accept</code> because that was the case I ran into. Caching successful <code>peer_addr</code> results makes sense too.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 627563571,
